message:
Fixed. `"Crème brûlée recipes"` now slugs to `creme-brulee-recipes`, and `npm test` passes all 3 tests.

The cause was the vendored `slugify`, which strips every character outside `a-z0-9`, so `è` and `û` were deleted rather than folded to `e` and `u`. I didn't touch `vendor/`, since its README says it's replaced wholesale on upgrades. Instead, `src/blog/slug.js` now decomposes the title (NFD) and removes the combining accent marks before calling slugify:

```js
// Split accented letters into base letter + combining mark, then drop the marks,
// so 'è' becomes 'e' instead of being removed by slugify.
exports.postSlug = (title) => slugify(title.normalize('NFD').replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, ''));
```

The shop's `src/shop/product-url.js` calls the same vendored slugify, so product names with accents will drop letters the same way. I left it alone because you scoped this to blog URLs. If you want it fixed too, the same two-line normalization would work there. I didn't commit anything.
